/*
 * ==========================================================================
 *  RECRUITMENT GORILLA: CANDIDATE IMPORT TEMPLATE
 * ==========================================================================
 *  Generated: {{GENERATED}}
 *
 *  These comments are instructions for the person, or the AI assistant,
 *  preparing this file. The importer ignores every comment, so you may keep
 *  them or delete them.
 *
 *  HOW TO USE
 *   1. Add one object per candidate inside the "candidates" array. A file can
 *      hold one candidate or many.
 *   2. Every candidate needs a CV file (PDF or DOCX, at most 10 MB).
 *   3. "cvFileName" must match the CV's file name exactly, including the
 *      extension, for example "jane_doe.pdf". Each CV is used once.
 *   4. In Recruitment Gorilla, open Upload CVs, choose "JSON + CVs", and drop
 *      this file together with all the CVs it lists.
 *   5. Each candidate becomes a Pending draft in the Review Workspace, where a
 *      reviewer checks the details and approves it.
 *
 *  MANDATORY FIELDS (an entry without these is rejected)
 *   - cvFileName : text, the CV's file name, e.g. "jane_doe.pdf"
 *   - fullName   : text, the person's name, at most 100 characters, with no
 *                  emoji or symbols
 *   - email      : text, a valid email address, e.g. "jane.doe@example.com"
 *
 *  OPTIONAL FIELDS (use null, or leave the key out, when unknown)
 *   - phone              : text, with country code, e.g. "+8801712345678"
 *   - currentTitle       : text, the candidate's current job title
 *   - relevantExperience : text, preferably one of:
 *                          {{EXPERIENCE}}
 *                          or a free value such as "4 Years"
 *   - location           : text, e.g. "Dhaka"
 *   - role               : the job opening applied for; must be one of the
 *                          ALLOWED ROLE NAMES below, spelled the same way.
 *                          Any other value is left blank for the reviewer.
 *   - source             : where the candidate came from; must be one of the
 *                          ALLOWED SOURCE NAMES below.
 *   - sourceDetail       : text, extra detail about the source
 *   - skills             : list of text, e.g. ["C#", "SQL", "React"]
 *   - summary            : text, a short professional summary
 *   - linkedInUrl, githubUrl, gitLabUrl, portfolioUrl, leetCodeUrl,
 *     codeforcesUrl, hackerRankUrl : full URLs starting with https://
 *   - educations  : list of { degree, institution, graduationYear, cgpa }.
 *                   degree and institution are required in each item.
 *   - experiences : list of { jobTitle, company, duration, description }.
 *                   jobTitle and company are required in each item.
 *                   duration is text, e.g. "Jan 2021 - Present".
 *
 *  ALLOWED ROLE NAMES (open job openings)
{{ROLES}}
 *
 *  ALLOWED SOURCE NAMES
{{SOURCES}}
 *
 *  RULES FOR AI ASSISTANTS FILLING THIS FILE
 *   - Return the whole file as JSON in exactly this structure. Keep the key
 *     names as written; do not rename keys or add new ones.
 *   - Use only information found in the CV or the data you were given. Never
 *     guess or invent values; use null when something is missing.
 *   - Write every value as text (in quotes), except skills, educations and
 *     experiences, which are lists.
 *   - Use exactly one object per CV, and set cvFileName to that CV's file name.
 *   - Copy role and source names exactly from the allowed lists above, or use
 *     null when none fits.
 * ==========================================================================
 */
{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "cvFileName": "jane_doe.pdf",
      "fullName": "Jane Doe",
      "email": "jane.doe@example.com",
      "phone": null,
      "currentTitle": null,
      "relevantExperience": null,
      "location": null,
      "role": null,
      "source": null,
      "sourceDetail": null,
